        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1f1f1f;" value="UNIVERSITY LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM — ENTITY-RELATIONSHIP DIAGRAM" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1400" x="40" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sub" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;" value="MIT8103 Advanced Database Systems · Portfolio 1 · Crow&#39;s foot notation" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="24" width="800" x="40" y="64" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;KEY&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;PK = primary key · FK = foreign key · UQ = unique · IDENTITY = automatically generated ID&lt;br&gt;NOT NULL = required · NULL = optional&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATIONSHIPS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each Book belongs to one Category. A Category has zero or many Books.&lt;br&gt;BookAuthor resolves the many-to-many relationship between Book and Author. Each BookAuthor row links one Book to one Author.&lt;br&gt;A Book has zero or many physical BookCopies. Each BookCopy belongs to one Book.&lt;br&gt;Each Loan refers to one BookCopy, one Student, and one Staff member. Each of these can be linked to multiple loan records over time.&lt;br&gt;A Loan has zero or one Fine. Fine.loan_id is both a foreign key and unique, allowing at most one Fine per Loan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;IMPORTANT RULES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Loan due_date must be on or after loan_date. return_date is optional and, when present, must be on or after loan_date.&lt;br&gt;The 14-day loan period is a business rule, not an enforced exact interval in the database.&lt;br&gt;A partial unique index prevents more than one active loan per physical copy. An active loan has return_date = NULL.&lt;br&gt;Book publication_year is optional and, when supplied, must be between 1000 and 2100.&lt;br&gt;BookCopy.copy_status is restricted to AVAILABLE, ON_LOAN, LOST, or DAMAGED.&lt;br&gt;Fine amount must be non-negative. amount_paid must be between zero and amount. Fine status is restricted to UNPAID, PARTIALLY_PAID, PAID, or WAIVED.&lt;br&gt;FineRate.daily_rate must be non-negative. effective_to is optional and, when supplied, must be on or after effective_from. A trigger rejects overlapping rate periods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;MODELLING LIMITATION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fine stores the calculated amount but does not reference FineRate or record which rate was applied. Fine calculations in the project are query-based examples, not automatic stored calculations.&lt;br&gt;A Book is not required to have an Author link or a physical copy." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="1000" x="40" y="930" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;CARDINALITY SYMBOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;|  exactly one&lt;br&gt;○|  zero or one&lt;br&gt;○&amp;lt;  zero or many" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="240" x="1100" y="930" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
